    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (80.64) leading the charge as our most confident start. Facing Bradley in a favorable environment, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a rare alignment of park factors and a slow delivery matchup that maximizes his elite speed\u2014the scarcest asset in our 5x5 framework. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Jose Caballero** (75.83) round out our top-tier targets; **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a prime matchup against Ure\u00f1a, where his power profile pairs perfectly with the park factor, while **Jose Caballero** exploits a high xERA arm in Abbott to provide significant value in the middle infield. **Seiya Suzuki** (71.48) also earns a strong recommendation, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Corbin elevates his ceiling well above the baseline.\n\nThe decision to bench **Zach McKinstry** (41.35) remains the most contentious call of the day. While his 41.35 efficiency score suggests he could survive in the utility slot, he ultimately fell short behind the broader consistency of **Max Muncy** (59.90), whose potential for production against Ure\u00f1a outweighs the marginal upside **Zach McKinstry** offers against Newcomb. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, further thinning our depth and emphasizing the need for **Dalton Rushing** and **Austin Riley** to maintain their discipline at the plate despite lower-than-ideal scores against challenging starters like Rogers and Harrison. With **Cole Young** falling just below our 40.0 floor, we are prioritizing our current starting nine to navigate the remaining game caps carefully.",
